{
  "0": "Across all four datasets, untie historical-input and candidate-output item embeddings. Initialize both tables identically, then train them independently; retain padding row zero and apply existing frequency attenuation only to historical inputs. Separate tables may resolve conflicting contextual and target-ranking gradients under pointwise logistic loss. Keep dimensions, features, causal backbone, readout, dot-product scoring, loss and optimizer unchanged. Update checkpoint loading and the predictor writer consistently; retain one model per category.",
  "1": "Across all four datasets, replace the first convolution's GELU branch in each NextItNet block with a gated causal convolution: produce 2H channels, split into a and b, and use a*sigmoid(b) before existing dropout and the second convolution. Learned gates may suppress irrelevant contextual signals more selectively than fixed residual scaling. Preserve dilations, residual addition, embeddings, features, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer. Update the predictor writer and checkpoint shapes consistently; retain one model per category.",
  "2": "Across all four datasets, jointly set Adam learning rate to 6e-4 and weight decay to 1e-5, retaining MAXLEN=64, hidden size 64, six blocks, dropout 0.15 and batch size 128. Smaller updates coupled with mild parameter regularization may improve generalization without repeating the previous simultaneous reductions in history length and dropout. Keep architecture, embedding parameterization, features, scoring, readout and loss unchanged; retain seed 42, at most 200 epochs and exactly 200 batches per epoch.",
  "3": "Across all four datasets, replace each scoring-position representation h_t with 0.8*h_t + 0.2*mean(h_j), averaging over the last four nonpadding encoder states ending at t, or all available states if fewer. Apply this causal pooling to every training target and use the final real position at inference. A small recent-context contribution may stabilize sparse histories while preserving the latest state's dominance. Keep history length, positions, embeddings, causal backbone, dot-product scorer, loss and optimizer fixed; synchronize the predictor writer."
}
